HISTORY OF MATHEMATICAL NOTATION
REFERENCE  |  types, variables, fundamentals
copy / share as plain text

THREE STAGES (Cajori / standard historiography)

RHETORICAL     everything in words
SYNCOPATED     abbreviations for unknown, power, minus
SYMBOLIC       letters + operators you manipulate as objects


NUMERALS  (place-value character)


TYPE           positional base-10  +  zero as a mark

FUNDAMENTALS   digit value = face * place
               place = power of base
               0 fills an empty place

PRIMARY TEXTS  Brahmagupta  Brahmasphutasiddhanta  (628)
               al-Khwarizmi  On Hindu Reckoning
               Fibonacci     Liber abbaci  (1202/1228)

MARKS          1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9  0  (zephir / sifr)
               older: Babylonian sexagesimal, Egyptian sign-value


PRE-SYMBOLIC ALGEBRA


TYPE           rhetorical algebra  /  syncopated algebra

FUNDAMENTALS   unknown determined by relation to knowns
               restoration + balancing  (al-jabr, al-muqabala)

PRIMARY TEXTS  Diophantus   Arithmetica     syncopated marks
               al-Khwarizmi Kitab al-jabr   almost no symbols
               al-Qalasadi                  Maghreb op-signs

VARIABLES      Diophantus: special glyph for unknown, sq, cube
               still not a general letter-script


LITERAL SYMBOLISM  (the modern algebraic page)


TYPE           species / literal algebra

FUNDAMENTALS   letter stands for a quantity
               known vs unknown distinguished by alphabet zone
               formula is an object you transform

VIETE 1591     In artem analyticem isagoge
  unknowns     vowels     A E I O U Y
  givens       consonants B G D ...
  constraint   homogeneity of dimension
               length*length written as area, not as number

HARRIOT 1631   Artis analyticae praxis
  marks        

DESCARTES 1637 La Geometrie
  unknowns     x y z     (end of alphabet)
  givens       a b c     (start of alphabet)
  powers       superscripts   x^2  x^3
  geometry     reduced to algebraic equations

STIFEL 1544    juxtaposition = multiply; word "exponent"


CALCULUS SCRIPTS  (competing characteristics)


TYPE           infinitesimal / fluxion / differential notation

LEIBNIZ        d x    d y / d x    integral sign
               design rule: the mark should suggest the act
               papers 1684, 1686  Acta Eruditorum

NEWTON         fluxions   x-dot    fluents
               Principia / De analysi
               historically huge, notationally the long-run loser

LATER RIVALS   Lagrange   f'(x)  f''(x)
               Euler      Delta for finite difference
               Condorcet  partial  d  (rounded) ~1770
               Cauchy     lim as an operator; eps-delta grammar

FUNDAMENTALS   increment of independent vs dependent
               differential as operator or as tiny quantity
               integral as inverse / as sum of products


EULER STANDARD  (18th c. page lock-in)


TYPE           analysis notation as common language

TEXTS          Mechanica 1736
               Introductio in analysin infinitorum 1748
               Institutiones calculi differentialis 1755

MARKS / VARS
  f(x)         function of an argument
  e            base of natural log
  pi           circle constant  (Jones 1706; Euler spreads it)
  i            sqrt(-1)         late Euler
  Sigma        summation
  sin cos tan  abbreviated trig
  log          logarithm
  A            finite difference  (with Bernoulli)

FUNDAMENTAL    a formula is a typed sentence in a shared alphabet


19th c. ANALYSIS GRAMMAR


TYPE           limit language  +  congruence  +  special functions

CAUCHY 1821    Cours d'analyse
  marks        lim   eps   delta
  idea         control the increment, do not trust the picture

GAUSS 1801     Disquisitiones arithmeticae
  mark         ===  congruence

WEIERSTRASS    classroom real-analysis script
ABEL / JACOBI  alphabets for elliptic / special functions


ARRAYS, MATRICES, DETERMINANTS


TYPE           tabular character for linear maps

MARKS          ( )  [ ]  | |  arrays
               det  as a single composed sign

TEXTS          Sylvester  1850  word "matrix"
               Cayley     1858  Memoir on the Theory of Matrices

VARIABLES      A B M     matrices
               a_ij      entry row i column j
               I         identity
               det A  |A|

FUNDAMENTAL    a rectangle of numbers is one object


VECTORS AND PRODUCTS  (notation war)


TYPE           directed quantity + two multiplications

HAMILTON       quaternions; one product; S and V parts
GRASSMANN      Ausdehnungslehre 1844/1862; outer product
GIBBS          Elements of Vector Analysis 1881-84
WILSON         Vector Analysis 1901  (Gibbs lectures)
HEAVISIDE      parallel vector calculus, other glyphs

GIBBS MARKS    bold a
               a . b     dot / scalar product
               a x b     cross / vector product
               nabla     gradient / del

INDEX / TENSOR
  Ricci-Levi-Civita   absolute differential calculus ~1900
  Einstein 1916       summation convention
                      repeated index = sum; Sigma dropped

VARIABLES      a_i      component
               g_ij     metric
               T^i_j    mixed tensor
               eps_ijk  Levi-Civita


SETS AND INFINITY


TYPE           collection as a primitive object

CANTOR         braces  { }     aleph  for cardinals
PEANO          in-symbol   union  intersection
               blackboard-bold drafts for N Q later standardized

MARKS          x in A
               A u B     A n B
               A subset B
               empty set
               |A| or card
               aleph_0

FUNDAMENTAL    membership is the basic verb


LOGIC AS A CHARACTER  (Leibniz program resumed)


TYPE           calculus of reasoning / ideography

BOOLE 1854     Laws of Thought     class algebra, still verbal
FREGE 1879     Begriffsschrift     2-D proof script; did not spread
PEANO          Formulario          linear marks that DID spread
RUSSELL        Principia 1910-13   Peano glyphs at book scale
HILBERT        Grundzuege 1928     cleaned first-order look
GODEL 1931     numbers that encode formulas
               notation about notation

COMMON MARKS
  ~  or  not
  /\   \/     and or
  ->       imply iff
  A x         for all
  E x         exists
  |-          proves
  |=          entails

VARIABLES      P Q R     propositions / predicates
               x y z     individuals
               F G       predicates
               Gamma     assumption set

FUNDAMENTAL    inference is a legal move on marks


